WEBVTT

00:00:00.400 --> 00:00:07.134
In this video, you will find displays that a professional lighting company installed, and look at the company behind them.

00:00:07.134 --> 00:00:08.229
We start on the map.

00:00:09.132 --> 00:00:10.881
Start at SoCal Lights dot app.

00:00:12.996 --> 00:00:15.514
On the home page, tap Use my location.

00:00:17.645 --> 00:00:18.627
Then tap Allow.

00:00:22.488 --> 00:00:23.811
Tap the season button.

00:00:26.750 --> 00:00:28.002
Pick the one you want.

00:00:28.002 --> 00:00:32.083
Christmas lights are the biggest, so tap Thanksgiving and Christmas Lights.

00:00:33.762 --> 00:00:37.196
Halloween, New Year, and other seasons are in the same list.

00:00:38.097 --> 00:00:39.163
Tap Filters.

00:00:41.156 --> 00:00:43.417
Under Type, tap Professionally installed.

00:00:45.093 --> 00:00:51.685
This shows only displays that a lighting company put up, which is great if you are thinking of hiring one for your own house.

00:00:52.584 --> 00:00:54.632
Tap the red button to show the places.

00:00:56.761 --> 00:00:58.262
Open one of the places.

00:00:58.262 --> 00:01:01.203
It says Installed by, with the company's name.

00:01:01.203 --> 00:01:04.206
A check mark means the company has confirmed it.

00:01:06.293 --> 00:01:08.704
Tap the company's name to open its profile.

00:01:10.777 --> 00:01:12.498
This is the company's profile.

00:01:12.498 --> 00:01:20.995
It lists where they work, their phone number, and their website, along with every display they have installed, so you can see their work before you call.

00:01:22.201 --> 00:01:24.483
Next up: Enter your home in a contest.
